; inputs: 0 1 4 9
; expect: 0 1 30 285
;
; `alloc` — the GATHER. A rule put in memory, pure and parallel by
; construction, as against `build`'s sequential scatter. A rule's parameter IS
; its domain (tables.md §6), which is what lets the body index the table it is
; built from; that was the third place the same sentence had to be applied and
; it was invisible until a stencil was written.
(def run (fn (n)
  (let (alloc (table (+ n 1) (fn (i) (* i i)))) (fn (t)
    (loop ((acc 0) (i 0))
      (>= i (len t))  acc
      else             (again (+ acc (t i)) (+ i 1)))))))
